{"content":"Found the root cause: in sqlparse/filters/reindent.py, `_next_token`'s recursion condition was inverted (`if not (token and token.normalized == 'BETWEEN'):`), which causes it to recurse on every normal split-keyword match instead of only when it hits a BETWEEN token — eventually recursing with `idx=None` and crashing in `token_next_by`'s `idx += 1`. Fixing the condition to `if token and token.normalized == 'BETWEEN':` restores correct behavior (skip past BETWEEN...AND without splitting there), and stops the runaway recursion for the normal case.","tool_calls":[{"id":"call_1","name":"replace_text","arguments":{"path":"sqlparse/filters/reindent.py","old_text":"        if not (token and token.normalized == 'BETWEEN'):
